======= 405c132 hybrid_handoff.c =======
commit 405c1321574f18229bab07b19a6548f56f8e537f
Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Fri Jun 12 19:46:40 2026 +0800

    behavioral: fcsr round-trips across the handoff (L20 resolved)

    fcsr (frm + sticky fflags) was in no transport surface: FP code inside
    the ROI ran with reset rounding (RNE) and the drained flags were stale.
    Now it rides every leg, gated on HYBRID_FLAG_FP:

    - wire format: uint64_t fcsr carved from reserved[] (216 -> 208 bytes,
      offset 3408 locked by state_abi_check.h). Pre-fix state files read
      back 0 = the old reset-value behavior, so no version bump.
    - QEMU1 drain: the plugin reads the fcsr gdbstub register alongside the
      FPRs.
    - vsim resume + drain: verilator submodule bump (ResumeDriver restore
      after the FPRs under the mstatus.FS enable; StateDrain read-back).
    - oracle: state-diff / run --verify compare fcsr under FLAG_FP.

    Proof: tests/fixtures/rt_c_fcsr.c sets fcsr=0x21 (frm=RTZ | NX) before
    the enter marker, self-checks the restored value inside the ROI on vsim
    (exits 1 on mismatch), then writes sentinel 0x45 for the exit drain.
    tests/hybrid/e2e_fcsr_roundtrip.sh asserts both drained file values;
    the fixture also runs in the marker/pc e2e suite (16/16 green, --verify
    e2e green).

    Docs: limitations notebook L20 -> RESOLVED (core-rule + state-coverage
    cells now say five restored CSRs, quickref + scorecard amended, live
    grep cell output refreshed); CLAUDE.md CSR-restore split + ABI summary;
    master ROADMAP F-ENG-04 -> DONE.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

