======= af39801 hybrid_handoff.c =======
commit af39801c74f9275e0c599b2f50eedb0d3f069b85
Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 16 16:25:53 2026 +0800

    behavioral: transport Andes cache CSRs across the QEMU->vsim handoff (L21)

    Add mcache_ctl (0x7CA) and mmisc_ctl (0x7D0) to the hybrid_state_v1 wire
    format (carved from reserved[], total size unchanged, no version bump),
    drain them in the QEMU plugin by gdbstub name, and bump the verilator
    submodule to the matching ResumeDriver restore.

    crt0 enables the L1 caches via mcache_ctl, but that write ran on the
    cache-less functional engine and was not carried over, so post-crt0
    hybrid windows resumed with caches disabled and ran uncached. hello
    main->_exit now drops 14707 -> 2871 cycles, below the whole-program
    cycle figure (3632) -- the correct subset relationship. Partially
    resolves L21 (the remaining Andes vendor CSRs are still not transported).

    Verified: host doctest suites + 43/43 e2e (marker + pc + neg, all
    --verify) pass.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

